# Deadline Octane Standalone Plugin - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is an AWS Thinkbox Deadline 10.4 render plugin for Octane Standalone. It enables farm rendering of Octane scenes (.ocs, .orbx files) with full control over output settings.

## Architecture

### Plugin Files (`plugins/Octane/`)
- `Octane.py` - Main Python plugin class, handles process execution and stdout parsing
- `Octane.options` - UI configuration for Deadline Monitor (dropdowns, checkboxes, text fields)
- `Octane.param` - System configuration (executable paths per version)
- `DeadlineOctane*.lua` - Lua render scripts executed by Octane Standalone

### Submission Script (`scripts/Submission/`)
- `OctaneSubmission.py` - Deadline submission dialog, creates job/plugin info files

## Coding Conventions

### Lua (Octane Scripts)
- Use `octane.*` namespace for all Octane API calls
- Prefer `octane.render.saveRenderPasses3()` over deprecated `saveRenderPasses()`
- Use `log(msg)` function with `io.stdout:flush()` for Deadline worker visibility
- Access render callback stats via `result.samples` and `result.maxSamples`
- Color space uses `PROPS_RENDER_COLOR_SPACE_INFO` structure
- Image format uses `octane.imageSaveFormat.*` enums

### Python (Deadline Plugin)
- Inherit from `DeadlinePlugin` class
- Use `self.GetPluginInfoEntry()` / `self.GetPluginInfoEntryWithDefault()` for job params
- Register stdout handlers with `self.AddStdoutHandlerCallback(regex)`
- Update progress with `self.SetProgress(percentage)` and `self.SetStatusMessage(text)`
- Log with `self.LogInfo()`, `self.LogWarning()`, `self.LogError()`

### Options File (.options)
- Use `[SectionName]` for UI groupings
- Types: `string`, `integer`, `float`, `boolean`, `enum`, `filename`, `folder`
- Labels appear in Deadline Monitor UI

### Param File (.param)
- System-level configuration (not per-job)
- Executable paths follow pattern: `Octane_RenderExecutable{VERSION}`

## Supported Versions
- Octane 4 (legacy)
- Octane 2019 (uses Octane 4 script)
- Octane 2026 (uses DeadlineOctane2026.1.lua)

## Testing Workflow
1. Submit test job from Deadline Monitor
2. Check worker log for stdout output
3. Verify progress bar updates in Monitor
4. Check rendered output files

## Common Patterns

### Adding New Render Option
1. Add entry to `Octane.options` with UI definition
2. Read value in `Octane.py` via `GetPluginInfoEntry()`
3. Pass to Lua script as command-line argument
4. Parse in Lua script and apply to render settings

### Updating for New Octane Version
1. Create new `DeadlineOctane{VERSION}.lua` based on latest
2. Add executable path to `Octane.param`
3. Add version to dropdown in `Octane.options`
4. Update version dispatch in `Octane.py`



